249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (A decade of building India's Formula Student engineers)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (Back in January 2017, more than 70 student teams from engineering colleges across India showed up at a race track in Coimbatore with cars they'd built themselves. That was the first Formula Bharat, India's answer to the Formula Student competitions that had been running abroad for decades, tracing back to 1981, when a University of Texas professor named Ron Matthews organised the very first Formula SAE race. That original idea eventually spread into 25 countries.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (The organisers, based in Mumbai, picked the Kari Motor Speedway in Coimbatore as their venue since it was affordable and able to host required events like the skidpad test. The track didn't have a skidpad at first. The owner, B Vijay Kumar, built one during a resurfacing the following year. Early challenges, per the same account, included language barriers and thin funding that relied on registration fees plus early sponsors, Altair Hyperworks and Bosch.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (Track talk: The evolution of formula Bharat)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
